{
  "sample": "internet-go-simplebank",
  "$comment": "Hand-labeled from the pinned sample source (scripts/samples.json, doc/** excluded: the generated statik bundle), not from Concentrate output. A gin API (api/), a gRPC server with a grpc-gateway HTTP mux (gapi/, main.go), sqlc queries on pgx (db/sqlc/) and an asynq worker; the Vue frontend/ is not labeled. Routes: the seven routes api/server.go registers (four on router.Group(\"/\").Use(authMiddleware(...)), which gin returns with the middleware) and the two net/http mounts runGatewayServer makes; the grpc-gateway patterns in the generated pb/*.pb.gw.go are not routes Concentrate is labeled for. Calls: every call site in the files listed whose callee is a function or method of this repository (generated pb getters and registration functions included), with the functions it runs; calls into gin, pgx, asynq, zerolog, grpc, gomock and the standard library, and calls of function values (fn, arg.AfterCreate, stop) are not labeled. A call on an interface is labeled with every type in the repository whose method set has the method with the same signature: db.Store with the sqlc Queries method SQLStore promotes (or SQLStore's own transaction method) and the gomock MockStore; worker.TaskDistributor with RedisTaskDistributor and the mock; token.Maker with JWTMaker and PasetoMaker; worker.TaskProcessor and mail.EmailSender have one implementer. q in the closures execTx is passed is a *Queries. Data access: each sqlc query method in db/sqlc/*.sql.go, by the table its SQL names (sqlc models are tables). Env: viper.Unmarshal in util.LoadConfig fills Config, whose mapstructure keys viper's AutomaticEnv reads from the environment. Scripts and infrastructure (scope: Makefile, Dockerfile, docker-compose.yaml, start.sh, wait-for.sh, eks/ and .github/; the frontend/ package.json is not labeled): entrypoints are the nineteen Makefile targets, the Dockerfile CMD and ENTRYPOINT, the three compose services, the three shell scripts and the two workflow jobs. RUNS: `server` runs main.go; the test job runs `make migrateup` and `make test`; the api service builds the Dockerfile; and, read as a person does, the Dockerfile ENTRYPOINT and the api service's `entrypoint:` run start.sh and wait-for.sh by their container paths (/app/start.sh, /app/wait-for.sh, copied by the Dockerfile). Env declarations: compose `environment:` (postgres and api) and the `env:` of the workflow's postgres service container and of the image build step; `docker run -e` in the Makefile and plain shell assignments (wait-for.sh's TIMEOUT, QUIET, PROTOCOL, HOST, PORT) are not declarations. SQL tables (sqlTables): the six tables the up migrations db/migration/000001\u2013000005 leave (down files are not read), read from the DDL by hand: columns in order with type as written (lower case), pk, unique and the references added by ALTER TABLE; the composite unique constraint on accounts(owner, currency) marks no column. Proto rpcs (rpcs): the four rpcs of pb.SimpleBank in proto/service_simple_bank.proto, each with its messages, the generated SimpleBankServer interface, and the gapi Server method that implements it, read from the .proto, pb/service_simple_bank_grpc.pb.go and gapi/.",
